{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979396363,"sessionID":"ses_1cc90dad7ffedWLI04NkShwCIr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_lnSvOimX2qz5qEyIyCKywS5x","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"Is this enough to make a disease association?\\nI ask, because I noted it locally in 2024, but it hasn't yet got an association.\\n\\n  | Functional studies in yeast confirm the pathogenicity of a new GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome variant.\\n  | PMID: 38773883 \",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach88AAAABAwxEpg\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"MeeSiing\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n10:       \"body\": \"Hi @ValWood we have MONDO:0980992 'Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9' which is associated with GINS3 gene. We can add 'GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome' as an exact synonym. Please let us know if you have any concerns. Thanks.\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-29T17:41:22Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n16:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933#issuecomment-4346102950\",\n17:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n18:     },\n19:     {\n20:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach88AAAABAw6E3w\",\n21:       \"author\": {\n22:         \"login\": \"ValWood\"\n23:       },\n24:       \"authorAssociation\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n25:       \"body\": \"I don't see it here:\\nhttps://monarchinitiative.org/HGNC:25851\\n\\nv\",\n26:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-29T18:02:20Z\",\n27:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n28:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n29:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n30:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n31:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933#issuecomment-4346250463\",\n32:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n33:     },\n34:     {\n35:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach88AAAABAxBePg\",\n36:       \"author\": {\n37:         \"login\": \"MeeSiing\"\n38:       },\n39:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n40:       \"body\": \"What I have said is based on OMIM reference in MONDO:0980992 'Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9', we have not included the gene association therefore you do not see it yet. \",\n41:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-29T18:18:58Z\",\n42:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n43:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n44:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n45:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n46:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933#issuecomment-4346371646\",\n47:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n48:     },\n49:     {\n50:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach88AAAABAxHHwQ\",\n51:       \"author\": {\n52:         \"login\": \"ValWood\"\n53:       },\n54:       \"authorAssociation\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n55:       \"body\": \"I dont understand?\",\n56:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-29T18:32:19Z\",\n57:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n58:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n59:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n60:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n61:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933#issuecomment-4346464193\",\n62:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n63:     }\n64:   ],\n65:   \"title\": \"GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome\",\n66:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933\"\n67: }\n\n(End of file - total 67 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"Is this enough to make a disease association?\\nI ask, because I noted it locally in 2024, but it hasn't yet got an association.\\n\\n  | Functional studies in yeast confirm the pathogenicity of a new GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome variant.\\n  | PMID: 38773883 \",\n  \"comments\": [\n    