{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979568316,"sessionID":"ses_1cc90dad7ffedWLI04NkShwCIr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_0hEIpZBdFeGKUkyLmBZog7WM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `MONDO:0980992` Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9 to add the missing GINS3 disease association, including a gene-based definition, exact synonym `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome`, and the germline mutation relationship supported by `PMID:38773883` and `OMIM:621512`.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Updated `MONDO:0980992` (`Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9`) to complete the expected gene-disease modeling for the GINS3-associated subtype discussed in issue `#9933`.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added a text definition following the MONDO `disease_series_by_gene` pattern: `Any Meier-Gorlin syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the GINS3 gene.`\n+- Added the exact synonym `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome`.\n+- Added logical axioms:\n+  - `intersection_of: MONDO:0016817 ! Meier-Gorlin syndrome`\n+  - `intersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851 ! GINS3`\n+- Added the asserted relationship:\n+  - `relationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851 {source=\"OMIM:621512\", source=\"PMID:38773883\"} ! GINS3`\n+- Added the issue tracker annotation linking back to `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933`.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue discussion showed that the relevant MONDO term already existed as `MONDO:0980992`, but it was missing the explicit GINS3 association and associated synonym, which is why the gene page did not yet surface the disease association.\n+- `PMID:38773883` is contextually appropriate: the PubMed record is titled `Functional studies in yeast confirm the pathogenicity of a new GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome variant` and describes Meier-Gorlin syndrome caused by biallelic `GINS3` variants.\n+- The edit aligns `MONDO:0980992` with the modeling already used for other Meier-Gorlin syndrome subtype terms in MONDO.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Reviewed existing Meier-Gorlin syndrome subtype stanzas in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` to match current MONDO modeling practice.\n+- Checked the relevant design pattern in `src/patterns/dosdp-patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml`.\n+- Verified the cited publication context via PubMed for `PMID:38773883`.\n+- Verified the parent term `MONDO:0016817` exists in the ontology.\n+- Ran a local syntax/serialization check:\n+  - `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n+\n+Notes:\n+- The repository guidance asks for ODK normalization via `make NORM`, but the containerized ODK path was not available in this environment because `docker` is not installed. I therefore completed the available local `robot convert` validation instead.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- [x] Read issue context and comments\n+- [x] Confirmed this was an update to an existing term, not a new term request\n+- [x] Checked relevant publication support\n+- [x] Applied MONDO gene-disease pattern to the existing term\n+- [x] Added issue tracker link\n+- [x] Ran local ROBOT syntax validation\n+- [x] Committed only `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>